{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ולא תחוס עינך עליו", :translit "v'lo tachus eincha alav", :gloss "and your eye shall not spare him"} {:he "אין טוענין למסית", :translit "ein to'nin l'masit", :gloss "one does not plead for a seducer"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ולא תחוס עינך עליו", :b "אין טוענין למסית"}], :frame {:text "A mesit (seducer) who incites others to idolatry is judged with unique stringency: if he left the court liable, they do not reopen his case to seek grounds for acquittal, unlike ordinary capital cases where the court seeks every avenue to acquit (Sanhedrin 81b). The phrase אין טוענין למסית expresses this rule.", :sources ["Sanhedrin 81b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ולא תכסה", :translit "v'lo t'chaseh", :gloss "and you shall not cover"} {:he "ולא תכסה עליו", :translit "v'lo t'chaseh alav", :gloss "and you shall not cover for him"} {:he "ולא תכסה עוד על הרוגיה", :translit "v'lo t'chaseh od al harugeihah", :gloss "and you shall not cover still for her slain"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ולא תכסה עליו" "ולא תכסה עוד על הרוגיה"]}], :frame {:text "The Sanhedrin is normally obligated to seek every possible ground to acquit someone facing a capital sentence, and if a new argument for acquittal emerges even after conviction, the court returns and reconsiders (Sanhedrin 32b, Sanhedrin 81b). A mesit is the exception: once he has left the court liable, they do not reopen his case. The phrase ולא תכסה עוד על הרוגיה is read as applying to one who goes out to be executed — i.e., once the seducer's verdict is sealed, do not 'cover' for him any further by seeking to reverse it.", :sources ["Sanhedrin 32b" "Sanhedrin 81b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ולא תחוס עינך עליו", :a-value 777, :b "אין טוענין למסית", :b-value 796, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ולא תכסה עליו" "ולא תכסה עוד על הרוגיה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ולא תכסה עליו", :refs ["Deuteronomy 13:9"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ולא תכסה עוד על הרוגיה", :refs ["Isaiah 26:21"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:29.253958154Z", :model "glm-5.2"}